# Working data. The Export button writes two files per run.
#
# redteam-lab-full-*.json  = EVERY row, including competition_restricted and
#                            employer_confidential. Never commit this.
# redteam-lab-*.jsonl      = filtered by disclosure class at export time.
#                            The default export is public rows only, which is the
#                            file that can safely become a published dataset.
#
# Default posture is to ignore both. When you deliberately want to publish a
# public-only export, force-add that one file:
#     git add -f logs/redteam-lab-2026-08-06.jsonl

logs/

# resources/ holds third-party OWASP PDFs (their copyright, not ours to
# redistribute) and an internal synthesis brief that maps them to a private
# engagement. Kept local, never published.
resources/

# Personal Obsidian vault config, not part of the tool.
.obsidian/

# Never, under any circumstances
*full*.json
.env
*.key
